 <p>
 Facebook stories disappear after 24 hours, but they don't have to be gone forever. TikSaveHub lets you
 <strong>download Facebook story videos in HD</strong> in seconds, free and without a watermark. Food tutorials
 from your favorite chefs, travel vlogs from creators you follow, announcements from brands you care about, or
 your own story that you want to keep. paste the link, tap Download, and the story is stored safely on your
 device, ready to watch offline any time.
 </p>

 <h3 class="text-highlight">How to save a Facebook story in HD</h3>
 <p>
 When you see a story you want to keep, open it and tap the share menu (the three dots or arrow) to copy its
 link. Then come back to TikSaveHub and paste the link into the box at the top of this page. Our servers fetch
 the story's media in seconds, and you get the HD or SD video with one tap. Because stories
 expire after a day, paste the link as soon as you see it; the download itself takes only moments.
 </p>

 <h3 class="text-highlight">HD 1080p quality, no watermark, every time</h3>
 <p>
 Our <strong>Facebook story downloader</strong> delivers the best resolution the story was uploaded in, up to
 1080p when available. We never re-encode, never compress, and never add an overlay, so the file you save is a
 faithful copy of the original. Prefer a smaller file? The SD option trims the size without ruining quality, and
 both options stay watermark-free.
 </p>

 <h3 class="text-highlight">Save stories on iPhone, Android, and desktop</h3>
 <p>
 Stories are consumed mostly on phones, so the tool is built mobile-first. On iPhone, paste the link into Safari
 and the video saves through your browser's download manager to the Files app. you can even export it to
 Photos. On Android, the MP4 lands in your gallery or Downloads folder. On a PC or Mac it drops into the
 download bar. Every screen gets large, thumb-friendly tap targets, so saving stories feels natural anywhere.
 </p>

 <h3 class="text-highlight">Photos too, and audio when you need it</h3>
 <p>
 Video stories download as MP4 in HD, and if you only want the soundtrack, the <a href="/facebook-to-mp3">Facebook
 to MP3 converter</a> handles any story video too. For photo-only stories, the platform doesn't expose a
 downloadable media stream, so a quick screenshot from your device remains the reliable route there. Everything
 else, every video story, is one link away.
 </p>

 <h3 class="text-highlight">Private, free, and unlimited</h3>
 <p>
 TikSaveHub works entirely in your browser: no app, no account, no email capture, and no stored history. The
 story is processed server-side and the only thing on your device is the final file. Downloads are unlimited and
 100% free, no caps, no premium tier, no surprises, so you can <strong>save Facebook stories to your device
 online</strong> as often as you like.
 </p>

 <p>
